glTF2: ImportEmbeddedTextures dereferences a NULL mimeType separator

Backport of upstream assimp commit 24bd7ee6 ("Fix glTF2 ImportEmbeddedTextures
NULL deref when mimeType has no '/'", PR #6733) -- merged after our pinned
release tag v6.0.5. Applied verbatim; it lands cleanly on the pin.

The bug
-------
    const char *ext = strchr(img.mimeType.c_str(), '/') + 1;
    if (ext) {

The null check is dead: when strchr returns nullptr the code has ALREADY
computed nullptr + 1, which is undefined behaviour and non-null, so the branch
is taken and every strncmp/strcmp below reads through the bogus pointer. The
mimeType string is file content -- a .glb whose image declares e.g.
"image" (no slash) reaches it.

Directly relevant to Jahshaka: embedded-texture extension handling is a path
we already patched around at our own layer (MaterialHelper::sniffImageExtension
exists because glTF mimeTypes lie), and .glb is the format the asset pipeline
suites exercise most.

The fix
-------
Test the separator, then form the extension pointer.

diff --git a/code/AssetLib/glTF2/glTF2Importer.cpp b/code/AssetLib/glTF2/glTF2Importer.cpp
--- a/code/AssetLib/glTF2/glTF2Importer.cpp
+++ b/code/AssetLib/glTF2/glTF2Importer.cpp
@@ -1720,8 +1720,9 @@ void glTF2Importer::ImportEmbeddedTextures(glTF2::Asset &r) {
         tex->pcData = reinterpret_cast<aiTexel *>(data);
 
         if (!img.mimeType.empty()) {
-            const char *ext = strchr(img.mimeType.c_str(), '/') + 1;
-            if (ext) {
+            const char *slash = strchr(img.mimeType.c_str(), '/');
+            if (slash != nullptr) {
+                const char *ext = slash + 1;
                 if (strncmp(ext, "jpeg", 4) == 0) {
                     ext = "jpg";
                 } else if (strcmp(ext, "ktx2") == 0) { // basisu: ktx remains
